## 🚀 Next Steps: Build Android APK

### Step 1: Install Capacitor (if not already installed)

```bash
npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli @capacitor/android
```

### Step 2: Sync Web Assets with Android

```bash
npx cap sync
```

This command will:
- Copy all files from `dist/` to Android project
- Update Capacitor configuration
- Prepare Android project for building

### Step 3: Build APK

#### Option A: Capacitor CLI (Recommended)
```bash
npx cap build android
```

#### Option B: Android Studio
```bash
npx cap open android
# Then click: Build → Build APK(s)
```

#### Option C: Gradle
```bash
cd android
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

